    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents argue that forcing interoperability fosters competition by preventing gatekeepers from locking users into single ecosystems, ultimately benefiting consumers with more choice. They suggest this breaks down monopolistic power and encourages innovation across different platforms. Conversely, opponents contend that mandated interoperability could stifle innovation by forcing companies to compromise on proprietary features or security. They also worry that it creates complex technical hurdles and could lead to degraded user experiences.",
